// `@tier` is a known directive written at the wrong site: it decorates the `fn` that runs a tier,
// never a type. It used to fall into the same "unknown directive `@tier`" message as a typo, which
// is a lie about a name the compiler knows — the author would hunt for a misspelling instead of
// moving the directive onto a function.
// expect: error E0003 at 7:2
// expect: exit 1
@tier(audit)
struct Report { lines: int }
echo "unreached"
